# Tailwind CSS v4 Development Guidelines

Best practices for using Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes effectively.

**Note**: Tailwind CSS v4 (released January 2025) uses a CSS-first configuration approach. If you need v3 compatibility, `tailwind.config.js` is still supported.

**NovelGuard bridge:** When styling web surfaces (docs sites, Canvas, future web UI), map semantic colors to tokens in [DESIGN.md](mdc:DESIGN.md). Do not invent ad-hoc hex — use `@theme` variables derived from the Calm SaaS palette. Follow **UX & UI principles** in DESIGN.md (layout, Morville criteria, dry-run safety).

## Core Principles

1. **Utility-First**: Use utility classes instead of custom CSS
2. **Mobile-First**: Design for mobile, then scale up with responsive modifiers
3. **Component Extraction**: Extract repeated patterns into components
4. **Consistent Spacing**: Use Tailwind's spacing scale
5. **Custom Configuration**: Extend the default theme for brand consistency

## NovelGuard @theme (from DESIGN.md)

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
    /* Dark (default) — see DESIGN.md colors */
    --color-background: #121212;
    --color-surface: #1e1e1e;
    --color-surface-elevated: #242424;
    --color-on-surface: #eaeaea;
    --color-on-surface-variant: #bdbdbd;
    --color-muted: #8a8a8a;
    --color-primary: #bb86fc;
    --color-secondary: #81d4fa;
    --color-selection: #3700b3;
    --color-outline: #2c2c2c;
    --color-hover: #2a2a2a;
    --color-error: #cf6679;
    --color-success: #80cbc4;

    /* Light — see DESIGN.md colors-light */
    --color-background-light: #fafafa;
    --color-surface-light: #ffffff;
    --color-primary-light: #6750a4;

    /* Typography — Pretendard per DESIGN.md */
    --font-family-sans: "Pretendard", "Noto Sans KR", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    --font-family-mono: Consolas, monospace;

    /* Radii — DESIGN.md rounded */
    --radius-sm: 6px;
    --radius-md: 12px;
    --radius-lg: 16px;

    /* Spacing — DESIGN.md spacing */
    --spacing-sm: 8px;
    --spacing-md: 16px;
    --spacing-lg: 24px;
}
```

Usage: `bg-background`, `bg-surface`, `text-on-surface`, `text-primary`, `rounded-md`, etc.

